Performance and readability (2026-07 audit)
===========================================

Measure first (before code changes):

- Baseline Top-N packages with --profile: ctx_union share, dep-model hit rate, reprove counters
  (prover:test_stats_pkgs + stats:test_stats_print_ctx_union_*; A/B config:dep_model_cache)

Tier A performance (only if measured):

- Specialized/indexed feature_unification:unify or narrower heuristic:should_union_ctx
- Ranking overlap precompute + cheaper dep-model choice-sig (keep hazard-encoded cache key)
- prove_recursive ctx-changed path: reuse sorted OldBody; share helpers with prove_model

Tier B performance (if reprove-heavy packages dominate):

- Incremental prune_model / prune_proof / prune_triggers (avoid full AVL rebuild)
- Safer prover:learn store update (nb_setval whole-AVL deep-copy concern


Security (2026-07 full-codebase audit)
======================================

Critical / High:

- [done] Rotate/remove committed HTTP digest password in Certificates/passwordfile
  — gitignored; `make passwordfile` derives hash from Private/passwords.pl

- [done] ebuild_exec:reactivate_toolchain/2 — process_create argv + Prolog chost parse
  (no sh -c); Major gated by sanitize:safe_path_component

- [done] ebuild_exec:register_ghc_pkg/1 — process_create argv (no sh -c)

- [done] explainer:call_llm/3 Pengines safelist gated by config:llm_server_calls/1
  (default false = host-local LLM; set true on trusted cluster to share server keys)

- [done] server:start_server bind scope
  — config:server_bind(localhost) default; require passwordfile; widen only on VPN
  (see 17-doc-distributed.md). mTLS+digest still required.

- [done] download:verify_hashes fails on empty Manifest checksum list

- [done] worker: Bonjour must match config:server_host pin; git:checkout requires
  full hex SHA already present locally (no fetch-from-server)


Medium:

- kernelconfig:build_apply_script — quote KDir/ConfigPath in sh -c (path metacharacters → RCE)
- download curl allows http/ftp; integrity depends on hashes (weakened by empty-checksum success)
- sandbox allows prover:learn/3 and worker post_result — poison shared-server prove state
- knowledgebase loads unsigned kb.qlf — write access to Knowledge/ is code exec
- resume.pl / feedback.pl read_term/3 with no integrity check — local writers poison plans
- config: missing Private/passwords.pl falls back to empty cert/digest passwords
  while public passwordfile remains

Low:

- sanitize docs say shell metacharacters OK for argv; several sh -c sites violate that contract
- default mirror_url is cleartext HTTP
- Certificates/*.pem public certs tracked (keys gitignored) — speeds attacks if CA key leaks
